{"pointer": "/scope_contracts/1/bidirectional_evidence/fact_consumer_chain/producer_context", "value": "Once a Fang secondary callback is actually reached and its internal chance is positive, it queries status eligibility first. Only an eligible status consumes its own status draw. The subsequent flinch draw is separate and still occurs when status is ineligible; it occurs before the Inner Focus rejection at flinch submission. The outer secondary-effect gate is a separate earlier draw; the default Thunder Fang outer chance is 101."}
{"pointer": "/scope_contracts/1/bidirectional_evidence/fact_consumer_chain/state_observation_and_later_result", "value": "Against an Electric target, paralysis eligibility is false before any status random draw. The first available internal random value 5 is consumed by flinch, so Flinch becomes true; 99 is not consumed inside that Fang callback. Reading “separately draw for status and flinch” as an unconditional pair instead consumes 5 on an impossible paralysis and 99 on flinch, producing false and shifting later random consumers."}
