{"pointer": "/scope_contracts/1/premises_and_counterexample/input_domain/2", "value": "Current mechanics use Electric-type paralysis immunity; actual target is pure Electric, remains alive, has no Inner Focus and no callback altering the status eligibility or counter."}
{"pointer": "/scope_contracts/1/premises_and_counterexample/input_domain/3", "value": "No additional chance modifiers: internal chance 10. All earlier accuracy/critical/variance/outer draws fixed separately; the next two available internal random values are 5, then 99."}
{"pointer": "/scope_contracts/1/premises_and_counterexample/ordinary_control", "value": "With an otherwise identical target that is not paralysis-immune, internal 5 produces paralysis, then internal 99 does not flinch. If status submission immediately cures the new status, that submission and its cure callbacks still happened before the flinch draw. Another independent control has active Inner Focus: the flinch draw is still consumed, but its commit is rejected."}
